A||N||7||reddog||bad shaking over 65mph||||1||
Z||000000||reddog||10-23-2001||05:34 AM||||Hello I just took my GT on a trip to a near by city. When I got on the interstate and got over 65mph I noticed a really bad vibration/ shaking that seemed to start in the steering and would work its way back to the rear. it would do this in a wave like effect constantly. (Front to Back) Occassionally in would all smooth out for a second in a slight curve to the left or right. I did a search just now and found that GTmike had the same problem but there was no post or reply that stated what it took to fix the problem.<BR>By the way I just put new 17" wheels and tires on my car Nankang 215/45/17 & 235/45/17 and have had them balanced twice so far! Someone please HELP!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fie Ro||10-23-2001||11:29 AM||||Bad balanced tires is what first comes to mind. I have exactly the same tyres, even the same sizes but i don't have problems with them. IF they are good balanced you should have a look at your suspension or your alignment... ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fie Ro||10-23-2001||11:39 AM||||Oh BTW: if you still have your old wheels put them on and see if the problem is still there. If it isn't then your new wheels are the problem.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||10-23-2001||12:06 PM||||Have the tires balanced or replaced.||||reg||1
Z||000004||gt boy||10-23-2001||12:24 PM||||try having the tires balanced on the car as opposed to off...sometimes there is another balancing problem with hubs,rotors or even the way the wheel fits on the studs.  find a shop that does this and you would not beleive the difference in the feel of the car.<P>------------------<BR>"it's too bad he had to run out of talent half way through the corner..."||||reg||1
Z||000005||reddog||10-24-2001||07:49 PM||||Thanks for the info. anybody else encountered this problem?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pictue87_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||varnster||10-24-2001||09:45 PM||||My 87 gt does it at about 80, I had it balanced and alighned ( new shocks) It is<BR>the tires on mine, their pretty worn and need<BR>replaced. The above did help a little but <BR>it didnt fix it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||reddog||10-24-2001||09:51 PM||||Well these are brand new Street Rebel wheels and Brand new tires. I am going to be pretty upset if its either of those. I just paid $1'100 for them. I am taking my GT to the shop tommorrow! I'll keep everyone posted!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||9
